<%
  usd = ->(v, digits = 0) { v.nil? ? "–" : number_to_currency(v, precision: digits) }
  pct = ->(v) { v.nil? ? "–" : number_to_percentage(v * 100, precision: 0) }
  mon = ->(m) { m.strftime("%b %Y") }
  k = @kpi
  card = "bg-container rounded-xl shadow-border-xs p-4"
  th = "text-left text-xs font-medium text-secondary px-2 py-1 whitespace-nowrap"
  td = "text-right text-sm text-primary px-2 py-1 whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums"
  tdl = "text-left text-sm text-primary px-2 py-1 whitespace-nowrap"
%>
<% content_for :page_header do %>
  <div class="space-y-1 mb-6">
    <h1 class="text-xl lg:text-3xl font-medium text-primary">Velocity</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-secondary">
      Whether you're spending above your means, judged on a normal month at your current pay (assumes your paychecks
      continue), and how money actually moved through your checking accounts month by month.
      Rent counts at your share everywhere in <%= product_name %>: each rent payment is split into your share and your roommate's, and the roommate's part and their Venmo are recorded as transfers.
    </p>
  </div>
<% end %>
<% nm = k[:nm]; badge = ->(ok) { ok ? %(<span class="mf-badge mf-ok">Verified</span>).html_safe : %(<span class="mf-badge mf-inf">Inferred</span>).html_safe } %>
<style>
  .mf-badge { font-size: 11px; border-radius: 9999px; padding: 1px 7px; white-space: nowrap; border: 1px solid currentColor; }
  .mf-ok { color: #0a7f0a; } .mf-inf { color: #a15c00; }
  html[data-theme="dark"] .mf-ok { color: #4cc24c; } html[data-theme="dark"] .mf-inf { color: #f0a841; }
</style>

<div class="space-y-6 pb-12">
  <div class="<%= card %>" style="border-left: 4px solid <%= k[:above_means] ? '#d03b3b' : '#0ca30c' %>">
    <p class="text-lg font-medium text-primary">
      <% if k[:above_means] %>
        ⚠ Above your means: a normal month at your current pay comes out <%= usd.(-nm[:left]) %> short of <%= usd.(nm[:take_home]) %> take-home.
      <% else %>
        ✓ Within your means: a normal month leaves <%= usd.(nm[:left]) %> of <%= usd.(nm[:take_home]) %> take-home (<%= pct.(nm[:savings_rate]) %> savings rate).
      <% end %>
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-secondary mt-1">
      At the higher card-spending rate (what you've actually paid Apple per month lately) it's <%= usd.(nm[:left_high]) %> a month.
      One-off purchases in the last 90 days, set aside: <%= usd.(nm[:one_offs]) %>, about <%= nm[:left].positive? ? "#{(nm[:one_offs] / nm[:left]).round} months" : "–" %> of a normal month's surplus.
      <%= link_to "Day-by-day forecast →", "/forecast", class: "underline" %>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
    <% [
      ["Take-home pay", usd.(nm[:take_home]), "per month: your paychecks as they arrive now"],
      ["Your costs", usd.(nm[:out]), "per month: rent share, bills, cards, everyday"],
      ["Left over", usd.(nm[:left]), "per month, in a normal month"],
      ["Savings rate on take-home", pct.(nm[:savings_rate]), "left over ÷ take-home pay"],
      ["Cash now", usd.(@cash_now), "checking accounts"],
      ["Runway, income continues", k[:runway_with_income] ? "#{k[:runway_with_income].round(1)} months" : "not burning", k[:runway_with_income] ? "cash now ÷ monthly shortfall" : "pay covers a normal month"],
      ["Runway, no income", k[:runway_no_income] ? "#{k[:runway_no_income].round(1)} months" : "–", "cash now ÷ your monthly costs"],
      ["Rent, your share", usd.(nm[:rent_share]), nm[:roommate].to_d.positive? ? "#{usd.(nm[:rent])} rent − #{usd.(nm[:roommate])} roommate Venmo" : "no roommate share found"],
      ["Card balances", usd.(@card_debt), "cards in #{product_name} (Discover, Apple Card)"],
      ["Velocity", k[:turnover] ? "#{k[:turnover].round(2)}× / month" : "–", "money out ÷ average cash, last 3 full months"],
      ["Days a dollar stays", k[:days_held] ? "#{k[:days_held].round} days" : "–", "average cash ÷ daily money out"],
      ["Spending, last 3 months", usd.(k[:spending]), "actual, per month, all accounts, rent at your share"]
    ].each do |label, value, hint| %>
      <div class="<%= card %>">
        <p class="text-xs text-secondary"><%= label %></p>
        <p class="text-xl font-medium text-primary tabular-nums"><%= value %></p>
        <p class="text-xs text-subdued"><%= hint %></p>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= card %> overflow-x-auto">
    <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-primary mb-2">A normal month at your current pay</h2>
    <table class="w-full">
      <tbody>
        <% rows = [["Take-home pay", nm[:take_home], true, "paychecks as they arrive now"],
                   ["Rent, your share", -nm[:rent_share], false, "rent minus your roommate's Venmo: the Venmo pattern is in the data, that it's your roommate's share is your figure"],
                   ["Recurring bills and subscriptions", -nm[:bills], true, @forecast.recurring.map { |r| "#{r[:name]} #{usd.(r[:amount], 2)}" }.join(", ")]] +
                  nm[:cards].map { |name, v| ["#{name} everyday spending", -v, false, "recent typical rate, one-offs left out" + (name =~ /apple/i ? "; includes its subscriptions" : "")] } +
                  [["Checking everyday spending", -nm[:everyday], false, "debit purchases and one-off Venmo, recent typical rate"]] %>
        <% rows.each do |label, v, ok, note| %>
          <tr class="border-t border-tertiary">
            <td class="<%= tdl %>"><%= label %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %>"><%= usd.(v) %></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1"><%= badge.(ok) %></td>
            <td class="text-xs text-secondary px-2 py-1"><%= note %></td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
        <tr class="border-t border-tertiary font-medium">
          <td class="<%= tdl %>">Left over (savings rate <%= pct.(nm[:savings_rate]) %>)</td><td class="<%= td %>"><%= usd.(nm[:left]) %></td><td></td>
          <td class="text-xs text-secondary px-2 py-1">at the higher card rate: <%= usd.(nm[:left_high]) %></td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-2">Card purchases count when you make them and card payments don't count, so nothing is counted twice. Every assumption is listed on the <%= link_to "Forecast", "/forecast", class: "underline" %> page.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="<%= card %> overflow-x-auto">
    <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-primary mb-2">Month by month, as it happened</h2>
    <% max = @months.map { |m| [@cash[m][:money_in], @cash[m][:money_out]].max }.max.to_f.nonzero? || 1 %>
    <table class="w-full">
      <thead><tr>
        <th class="<%= th %>">Month</th><th class="<%= th %>">Money in</th><th class="<%= th %>">of which pay</th>
        <th class="<%= th %>">Money out</th><th class="<%= th %>">of which card payments</th><th class="<%= th %>">Net</th>
        <th class="<%= th %>">Savings rate on pay</th><th class="<%= th %>">Spending (all accounts)</th><th class="<%= th %>">vs last month</th>
        <th class="<%= th %>" style="min-width:160px">in / out</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <% @months.reverse.each_with_index do |m, i| c = @cash[m]; net = c[:money_in] - c[:money_out]
           prev = @spend_by_month[m << 1]; spend = @spend_by_month[m] %>
          <tr class="border-t border-tertiary">
            <td class="<%= tdl %>"><%= mon.(m) %><%= " (so far)" if i.zero? %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %>"><%= usd.(c[:money_in]) %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %> text-secondary"><%= usd.(c[:income]) %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %>"><%= usd.(c[:money_out]) %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %> text-secondary"><%= usd.(c[:card_payments]) %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %>" style="color: <%= net.negative? ? '#d03b3b' : '#0ca30c' %>"><%= usd.(net) %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %>"><%= c[:income] >= 1000 ? pct.(net / c[:income]) : "–" %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %>"><%= usd.(spend) %></td>
            <td class="<%= td %> text-secondary"><%= prev && prev.nonzero? ? number_to_percentage((spend - prev) / prev * 100, precision: 0, format: "%n%").sub(/\A(?!-)/, "+") : "–" %></td>
            <td class="px-2 py-1">
              <div style="height:6px;background:#0ca30c;border-radius:3px;width:<%= (c[:money_in].clamp(0, max) / max * 100).round(1) %>%"></div>
              <div style="height:6px;background:#d03b3b;border-radius:3px;margin-top:2px;width:<%= (c[:money_out].clamp(0, max) / max * 100).round(1) %>%"></div>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="text-xs text-subdued mt-2">
      Money in/out: checking only, moves between your accounts left out, and the roommate's share of rent and their
      Venmo left out (recorded as transfers). Card payments are money out (that's when card spending leaves your cash),
      including cards not in <%= product_name %>. Savings rate on pay: net ÷ pay that month (blank when there was little or no pay).
      Spending: purchases minus refunds on every account, rent at your share; transfers and card payments left out.
    </p>
  </div>

  <% [["Spending by category", @categories], ["Top merchants", @merchants]].each do |title, list| %>
    <div class="<%= card %> overflow-x-auto">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-primary mb-2"><%= title %> (net of refunds)</h2>
      <table class="w-full">
        <thead><tr>
          <th class="<%= th %>"><%= title.include?("merchant") ? "Merchant" : "Category" %></th>
          <% @months.last(7).each do |m| %><th class="<%= th %> text-right"><%= mon.(m) %></th><% end %>
          <th class="<%= th %> text-right">last 12 full months</th><th class="<%= th %> text-right">per month</th>
        </tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% list.each do |row| %>
            <tr class="border-t border-tertiary">
              <td class="<%= tdl %>"><%= row[:name].to_s.truncate(32) %></td>
              <% @months.last(7).each do |m| %><td class="<%= td %>"><%= row[:months][m] ? usd.(row[:months][m]) : "" %></td><% end %>
              <td class="<%= td %> font-medium"><%= usd.(row[:total]) %></td>
              <td class="<%= td %> text-secondary"><%= usd.(row[:total] / @full_months.size) %></td>
            </tr>
          <% end %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <p class="text-xs text-subdued">
    Recurring charges and subscriptions: <%= link_to "Recurring", "/recurring_transactions", class: "underline" %>.
    Built-in charts: <%= link_to "Dashboard", root_path, class: "underline" %> (net worth, cash flow) and
    <%= link_to "Reports", "/reports", class: "underline" %> (income vs expenses, trends, budgets).
  </p>
</div>
